.TH LINSPEC 1 "2026-06-27" "LinSpec" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linspec \- Linux kernel hardening audit tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linspec
[\fI--json\fR | \fI--csv\fR | \fI--html\fR]
[\fI--apply\fR]
[\fI--profile\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fI--watch\fR]
[\fI--help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
LinSpec performs 29 kernel hardening checks across 7 categories:
memory protection, kernel configuration, network hardening,
filesystem security, CPU mitigations, cryptographic settings,
and execution restrictions. It reads /proc/sys and /sys
interfaces and compares values against known secure baselines.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \--json
Export results in JSON format.
.TP
.B \--csv
Export results in CSV format.
.TP
.B \--html
Export results in HTML report.
.TP
.B \--apply
Apply recommended sysctl remediations (requires root).
.TP
.B \--profile \fIname\fR
Load a named hardening profile from profiles/ directory.
.TP
.B \--watch
Monitor sysctl values continuously for changes.
.TP
.B \--help
Display this help message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I profiles/
Directory containing named hardening profiles.
.TP
.I reports/
Output directory for audit reports.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, 1 on error.
.SH AUTHOR
Jefferson Cesar Antunes
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kscanner (1),
.BR kverify (1),
.BR syscage (1)
